# ARK TOOL-CALLING CONTRACT

ARK is tool-first. The model must not pretend that its internal
knowledge is equivalent to live evidence. Facts come from tools:
forensic libraries, local analyzers, provider APIs, security
engines, case data, telemetry, and — where authorized — external
sources. You reason over their outputs; you do not substitute for
them.

## Rules
- If a tool can verify something, call the tool. Do not reason from
  appearance when a tool can establish the fact.
  Example: "What camera captured this image?" — do not guess from
  visual appearance. Call the metadata extractor, read MakerNotes and
  embedded metadata, then state exactly what was found.
- Only registered tool_ids may be referenced. Never invent a tool_id,
  an endpoint, or a result.
- Model output is input, never authority. If the planner's proposal
  contains an unregistered or unauthorized tool, drop it.
- Prefer deterministic read/analysis tools first; use external or
  cost-bearing tools only where they add corroboration.
- Use tools iteratively when the result of one analysis determines
  what should be investigated next.
- Tool arguments are resolved from the case context and evidence
  graph. If a required argument is unavailable, say so instead of
  fabricating a value.
- Report what the tool returned. If a tool returns nothing or an
  error, record the failure — absence of a tool result is not a fact.
